  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We prove Hanna's conjecture in OEIS A389474, FORMULA (3), and the companion conjectures in A389474, FORMULA (4), A389475, FORMULA (4.a), (4.b), and A389472, COMMENTS. For the first equation we establish A(x)^2 = x^2 + 2x^3 + 9Q(x), with Q in Z[[x]]. Integral coefficient constructions, Frobenius and binomial descent prove the six congruences. We also establish reversion identities and every even-power congruence modulo nine. If D is the A350432 series, every rational-seed solution of the A389472 equation is C_s=x+sD^2. Its product representation proves the stated convergence radius (sqrt(5)-1)/2 for D and every C_s with s nonzero.",
